      "kind": "review",
      "heading": "‘The Dog Stars’",
      "films": [
        {
          "title": "The Dog Stars",
          "year": 2025,
          "note": "Ridley Scott's post-flu-pandemic thriller from Peter Heller's novel, adapted by Mark L. Smith. Elordi is Hig and Brolin is Bangley at a Colorado airfield (shot in Italy). The aerial photography is beautiful and the pacing is dead on arrival; the Carhartt stays immaculate. The Grand Junction cannibal-colony turn is a film invention absent from the book."
        }
      ]
